<surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernad</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanco</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA polymerase mu (Pol mu), homologous to TdT, could act as a DNA mutator in eukaryotic cells</article-title><source>EMBO J.</source><year>2000</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1731</fpage><lpage>1742</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10747040</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bertocci</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>De Smet</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Berek</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Weill</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynaud</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Immunoglobulin kappa light chain gene rearrangement is impaired in mice deficient for DNA polymerase mu</article-title><source>Immunity</source><year>2003</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>203</fpage><lpage>211</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12932354</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bertocci</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>De Smet</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Weill</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynaud</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonoverlapping functions of DNA polymerases mu, lambda, and terminal deoxynucleotidyltransferase during immunoglobulin V(D)J recombination in vivo</article-title><source>Immunity</source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16860755</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Daley</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Laan</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Suresh</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA joint dependence of pol X family polymerase action in nonhomologous end joining</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>2005</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>29030</fpage><lpage>29037</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15964833</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tippin</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimazaki</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Lieber</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>XRCC4:DNA ligase IV can ligate incompatible DNA ends and can ligate across gaps</article-title><source>EMBO J.</source><year>2007</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>1010</fpage><lpage>1023</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17290226</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Juarez</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiz</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>McElhinny</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramsden</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanco</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A specific loop in h